  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over a strong unimodal baseline. Config_002 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is the simplest possible RNA-only configuration—no fusion, no aggregation, single profile—making it a clean reference floor. scvi_n200 is a well-established, robust single-cell RNA encoder, so this experiment isolates the question 'How well can we classify using RNA alone?' without confounding variables. Establishing this baseline first is essential: any subsequent multimodal result can only be interpreted as a gain (or lack thereof) relative to this number. It directly operationalizes the principle of not assuming complex multimodal models will outperform simpler ones, and it reduces the greatest uncertainty in the search space before investing experiments in more complex configurations."
}

